umiproc patch 0012: read-only System::GetAtlas()

What: a public inline System::GetAtlas() returning the atlas pointer (System keeps owning it), and the macro
UMIPROC_SYSTEM_GET_ATLAS so a front-end can tell a build that has it. umiproc_slam --save_points reads the biggest
map's points and keyframes through it after Shutdown().
Why: System keeps the atlas private (mpAtlas) and the fork has no accessor; the front-end's earlier prototype read
the private member with the explicit-instantiation access idiom, which this replaces.
Behaviour change: none (header only; nothing in the library calls it).

diff --git a/include/System.h b/include/System.h
index 5cc4b95..f92f95e 100644
--- a/include/System.h
+++ b/include/System.h
@@ -213,6 +213,11 @@ public:
     float GetImageScale();
     bool isLoadingMap();
 
+    // umiproc patch 0012: read-only access to the atlas (its maps, keyframes and map points), for umiproc_slam's map
+    // export. Call it after Shutdown(), when no thread changes the atlas any more; the System keeps owning it.
+#define UMIPROC_SYSTEM_GET_ATLAS 1
+    Atlas* GetAtlas() const { return mpAtlas; }
+
 private:
 
     void SaveAtlas(int type);
